{
  "text": "This review adds a pull request gate for parcel notices. Start with the changed paths on the left, then follow selection, source validation, translation comparison, and the final check status. An English text edit brings its language variants. A direct translation edit selects one notice. Shared code changes, or a manual full audit, select the whole catalog. The catalog has two relationships: source identity and input contract. Crossing this boundary means a notice was actually selected for validation. The runner resolves English and loads the allowed input contract for each selected entry. An empty list never crosses this boundary. Allowed names come from shared inputs, direct inputs, and derived values. The item table is produced before rendering, but remains legal in a template. Partner overrides use the same contract as their base notice. English must parse and use known input names. A broken source goes straight to the failure report for that notice. A valid English only entry is done. A translated entry continues down to comparison. The translation must retain the subject, preview, and body fields, with the same placeholder sets in each. Moving the item table into another field fails. These checks prove syntax and input parity, not the meaning of the translated prose. Any file issues make the check fail. The runner still gathers the remaining results. The lower feedback path is a human action: edit the source or selection logic and submit another revision. There is another route. A contract only edit matches no selection branch, so the scoped run checks zero notices and passes. That empty selection is the false green path, even though five notices depend on the changed contract. The same edit fails five notices in a full audit. That confirms the validator works and selection is incomplete. The fix is to follow the contract relationship to every consumer, including partner overrides. The reproduction is included in the source.",
  "beats": [
    {
      "target": "changes",
      "title": "Start with changed paths",
      "text": "This review adds a pull request gate for parcel notices. Start with the changed paths on the left, then follow selection, source validation, translation comparison, and the final check status.",
      "start": 0.0,
      "charStart": 0
    },
    {
      "target": "selector",
      "title": "Select the right work",
      "text": "An English text edit brings its language variants. A direct translation edit selects one notice. Shared code changes, or a manual full audit, select the whole catalog. The catalog has two relationships: source identity and input contract.",
      "start": 12.75,
      "charStart": 193
    },
    {
      "target": "selected",
      "title": "Coverage boundary",
      "text": "Crossing this boundary means a notice was actually selected for validation. The runner resolves English and loads the allowed input contract for each selected entry. An empty list never crosses this boundary.",
      "start": 28.9,
      "charStart": 432
    },
    {
      "target": "contract",
      "title": "Three input sources",
      "text": "Allowed names come from shared inputs, direct inputs, and derived values. The item table is produced before rendering, but remains legal in a template. Partner overrides use the same contract as their base notice.",
      "start": 42.95,
      "charStart": 641
    },
    {
      "target": "english",
      "title": "English comes first",
      "text": "English must parse and use known input names. A broken source goes straight to the failure report for that notice. A valid English only entry is done. A translated entry continues down to comparison.",
      "start": 57.725,
      "charStart": 855
    },
    {
      "target": "translation",
      "title": "Compare each field",
      "text": "The translation must retain the subject, preview, and body fields, with the same placeholder sets in each. Moving the item table into another field fails. These checks prove syntax and input parity, not the meaning of the translated prose.",
      "start": 71.525,
      "charStart": 1055
    },
    {
      "target": "fail",
      "title": "Collect issues, then repair",
      "text": "Any file issues make the check fail. The runner still gathers the remaining results. The lower feedback path is a human action: edit the source or selection logic and submit another revision.",
      "start": 87.05,
      "charStart": 1295
    },
    {
      "target": "empty",
      "title": "The bypass matters",
      "text": "There is another route. A contract only edit matches no selection branch, so the scoped run checks zero notices and passes. That empty selection is the false green path, even though five notices depend on the changed contract.",
      "start": 99.8,
      "charStart": 1487
    },
    {
      "target": "finding",
      "title": "Verify the finding",
      "text": "The same edit fails five notices in a full audit. That confirms the validator works and selection is incomplete. The fix is to follow the contract relationship to every consumer, including partner overrides. The reproduction is included in the source.",
      "start": 115.025,
      "charStart": 1714
    }
